---
import PageLayout from '../../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Knowledge Base', href: '/knowledge' },
  { label: 'How to Choose a CNC Supplier' },
];

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: 'How to Choose a CNC Supplier (Overseas Buyer Guide)',
  description: 'What overseas buyers should vet before committing: nameplate-verified machines, first-pass yield, material traceability, commercial red-lines and failure-path transparency.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Eternal CNC Precision Machining' },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Eternal CNC Precision Machining',
    logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://www.eternalcnc.com/images/og-default.webp' },
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': Astro.url.href },
  inLanguage: 'en',
};
---

<PageLayout
  title="How to Choose a CNC Supplier | Overseas Buyer Guide | Eternal CNC"
  description="How overseas buyers should vet a CNC shop: nameplate-verified machines, first-pass yield, material traceability, commercial red-lines and failure-path transparency."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  schema={articleSchema}
>
  <style>
    .sc-card { background: var(--card-white); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left: 4px solid var(--brand-red); padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; color: #374151; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; }
    .sc-card h3 { color: var(--brand-dark); margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 17px; }
    .sc-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 16px 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .sc-table th, .sc-table td { border: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding: 12px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #374151; }
    .sc-table th { background: var(--page-bg); color: var(--brand-dark); font-weight: 600; }
    .sc-table tr:nth-child(even) { background: #FAFAFA; }
    .sc-quote { background: var(--page-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left: 4px solid var(--brand-red); padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; color: #374151; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; font-style: italic; }
  </style>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--card-white); padding: 80px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-3" style="color: var(--brand-red);">Knowledge Base</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-5" style="color: var(--brand-dark);">
        How to Choose a CNC Supplier
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg max-w-3xl leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--text-body);">
        Overseas buyers don't choose a CNC shop by price or reply speed. They choose one that stays qualified — a real factory,
        stable yield, traceable material, and honest about what happens when things go wrong. Here's the due-diligence checklist we'd use if we were in your shoes.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-8">
        <a href="/contact/get-a-quote" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium bg-[#8B0000] text-white rounded transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-[#6B0000] hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          Request a Quote
        </a>
        <a href="/downloads/EternalCNC-Supplier-Ethics-EN.html" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium border border-[#8B0000] text-[#8B0000] rounded-md transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-[#8B0000] hover:text-white hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          Download Print-Ready Guide ↓
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 1 real factory -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--page-bg); padding: 72px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2" style="color: var(--brand-red);">1 · Real factory</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--brand-dark);">Real Machines, Real Nameplates</h2>
      <p class="max-w-3xl mb-6" style="color: var(--text-body);">
        A pretty storefront on a B2B platform is not a factory. A trader reselling someone else's capacity is not a factory.
        Ask for a video tour with the camera on the nameplate of the actual machine running your drawing — brand, model, serial number, calibration-label date.
        A trader can't show you "the machine + the G-code screen currently running your part." That single check filters out most middle layers.
      </p>
      <div class="sc-card">
        <h3>What we do</h3>
        Our 24 machining centers are nameplate-verified, calibrated quarterly. Our About page carries a "nameplate wall" gallery (sensitive data masked) — far more convincing than the words "real factory."
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 not cheapest -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--card-white); padding: 72px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2" style="color: var(--brand-red);">2 · Value, not price</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--brand-dark);">Cheapest + Fastest Reply = Two Red Flags</h2>
      <p class="max-w-3xl mb-6" style="color: var(--text-body);">
        Low price + instant reply usually means one of two things: (a) your order gets subcontracted to a small workshop, or (b) they'll cut corners on material, tolerance or inspection.
        What's actually valuable is the <strong>stability</strong> of turning drawings into qualified parts — first-pass yield, rework rate, batch-to-batch consistency.
        Seasoned buyers look at "average PPAP / first-article pass rate over the last 10 batches," not "this quote is 8% cheaper."
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 stable delivery -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--page-bg); padding: 72px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2" style="color: var(--brand-red);">3 · Stable delivery</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--brand-dark);">Three Things That Make Delivery Stable</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="sc-card"><h3>No deformation</h3>Tolerances hold, thin walls don't warp, deep holes don't drift; critical-dimension reports (CMM available on request) match what you measured.</div>
        <div class="sc-card"><h3>No material swap</h3>6061-T6 stays 6061-T6 — never quietly swapped for 6061-O or recycled aluminum. All materials sourced exclusively from certified mills; EN 10204 3.1 mill certs available on request, heat-number bound and fully traceable end to end.</div>
        <div class="sc-card"><h3>They cooperate</h3>DFM feedback ("this 10×D hole — suggest drilling from both sides"), drawing questions answered within 24h, you can specify grade and source.</div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl" style="color: var(--text-body);">
        <strong>On rush jobs:</strong> the right shop is transparent about current machine load. If it has free capacity, it takes the rush; if it's full, it tells you honestly it'll slip. That shop is the one you can commit to long-term.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 commercial red-lines -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--card-white); padding: 72px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2" style="color: var(--brand-red);">4 · Commercial red-lines</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--brand-dark);">Six Red-Lines Buyers Should Set</h2>
      <table class="sc-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Your red-line</th><th>What it means in practice</th><th>What we do</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Full material traceability</td><td>Source exclusively from certified mills; EN 10204 3.1 certification available on request; no verbal "material guarantee" accepted</td><td>Strict heat-number binding and batch archiving; every delivered batch is traceable to its original MTC and mechanical properties</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Quote within 24h</td><td>Not an instant number — a segmented quote (machining + finish + QC + packing + freight) within 24h; DFM depth scales with RFQ completeness and buying intent</td><td>Three-tier response: rough estimate for budget checks; quote + key DFM summary when drawings are provided; full DFM report for high-intent/prototype projects</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bilingual NDA</td><td>Mutual NDA in EN+CN; accept your NDA version</td><td>Mutual NDA, EN/CN, bidirectional</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Drawing handling</td><td>Encrypted storage; returnable/destroyable on project end; not reused for third parties</td><td>Written into NDA clause 4 + isolated drawing directory</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Paid first-article</td><td>Sample charged (no free trial); same process as production; sample report first</td><td>1–5 pcs paid sample, FAI first</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Deposit + balance on inspection</td><td>No 100% prepayment; 30–50% deposit + 50–70% on final inspection / shipment report</td><td>Fixed staged-payment terms on every quote; CMM reports available on request from our group's shared metrology center</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="sc-card mt-5 max-w-3xl">
        <h3>Why tiered DFM?</h3>
        We don't treat a full DFM as an unconditional giveaway. Budget-check inquiries receive a rough estimate; evaluation buyers with drawings receive a standard quote with key risk notes; only high-intent or prototype projects trigger a full DFM, fixture plan and tolerance analysis from engineering. This keeps our 24-hour promise while protecting engineering capacity from price-shopping RFQs.
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl" style="color: var(--text-body);">With these six in place, most overseas buyers move you from "candidate" to "qualified supplier list" — even if your unit price isn't the lowest.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 failure-path transparency -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--page-bg); padding: 72px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2" style="color: var(--brand-red);">5 · Failure-path transparency</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--brand-dark);">The Difference a Real Factory Won't Hide</h2>
      <p class="max-w-3xl mb-6" style="color: var(--text-body);">
        The biggest gap between a trader and a real factory: traders only talk about successful samples; a real factory talks about <strong>what happens when it goes wrong</strong>.
        Put these in your order terms attachment — far more useful than "quality first."
      </p>
      <div class="sc-card mb-4"><h3>First-article out of tolerance</h3>Who pays rework? What's the rebuild lead time? Who pays freight?</div>
      <div class="sc-card mb-4"><h3>Wrong material found in batch</h3>Recall mechanism? Compensation terms?</div>
      <div class="sc-card"><h3>Delivery delay</h3>How many days' notice? Is there backup capacity?</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- quote -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--card-white); padding: 72px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2" style="color: var(--brand-red);">In our words</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--brand-dark);">Why Buyers Stay With Us</h2>
      <div class="sc-quote">
        Most buyers don't choose a CNC shop by price or reply speed. They stay because the shop is a real factory with nameplate-verified machines, turns drawings into qualified parts with low rework, never swaps material grades, and still picks up the phone on a rush order. We run 24 CNC centers (DMU 400 + Taikan lineup), calibrate quarterly, provide EN 10204 3.1 mill certs on request, and make dimensional reports — including CMM reports via our group's shared metrology center — available on request. We return a tiered quote and DFM feedback within 24 hours based on RFQ completeness, sign bilingual mutual NDA, isolate customer drawings, charge for first-article samples, and work on 30–50% deposit + balance against inspection report — no 100% prepayment. That's not a sales pitch; it's how we've avoided becoming a ghost supplier.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--brand-dark); padding: 80px 0;">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-5">Ready to Qualify a Supplier?</h2>
      <p class="text-lg mb-8" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">
        Send us your drawing and project context. We'll return a tiered segmented quote and DFM feedback matched to your intent, plus a mutual NDA, within 24 hours.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/contact/get-a-quote" class="inline-block px-8 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold bg-[#8B0000] text-white rounded transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-[#6B0000] hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          Request a Quote
        </a>
        <a href="/knowledge" class="inline-block px-8 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold border border-white/30 text-white rounded-md transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-white hover:text-[#8B0000] hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          View All Resources →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
